h  a good friend to get his audition tape  done and he didn't hold back in bringing  the character frenchie to life he  screamed his lungs out in french take  after take but since they were filming  outdoors people nearby heard and got  worried next thing the after knew his  tape was interrupted by five undercover  cops raiding his yard one of the cops  who charged forward quickly recognized  the actor though and they stood down  tomer was much more careful after that  confessing i may have forgotten for a  moment where i live luckily i got the  job so we guessed the trouble was worth  it yeah i was aesthetic and hypnotic and  amazed by this guy number four  auditioning for the boys was a  surprisingly electrifying experience  quaid shared that aaron was the first  person to get cast and my first callback  was with her a chemistry read and our  first time ever meeting however his  second was the one that really shook him  the actor had a hard time articulating  exactly what it was like saying that was  the most surreal thing that's ever  happened in my life it was memorable to  say the least you know when i got cast i  i couldn't really believe it i i still  can't kind of can't believe it number  five this show was still a mystery when  the season two auditions began  ayakosh was intrigued but she wanted to  have a chat with the director first  since auditions were underway cash was  just given a longer audition time slot  to chat with kripke and while it all  went well enough cash wasn't confident  since everyone else she saw auditioning  looked very different from her but she  was proven wrong much to her delight  thing about stormfront is she's not  afraid of anybody which i think makes  her unique number six good friends tell  friends about auditions chase crawford  got lucky with his pals who mentioned he  should look into the project he pitched  it to his agent and they got him in but  his hopes weren't up when he saw about a  hundred other people auditioning 